#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9466d5b-d361-5504-8e16-99f87210e808" :knowledge-point/title "The Singular Value Decomposition of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d3ea076-4d0b-50b5-af4f-ca0b0399c71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495613} {:answer/id #uuid "3143f9ac-e07a-56d2-986f-b0a7f64340bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495622} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3656be-5473-5356-8bab-68c6041eb7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495651} {:answer/id #uuid "5afcdc04-e77f-5dcd-84c4-8d2f63b67107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495716} {:answer/id #uuid "90a84480-b5fe-5e99-a5ca-05d902ef19d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3143f9ac-e07a-56d2-986f-b0a7f64340bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495622} :answer-field/id #uuid "20030bd4-6e8a-5215-b9ee-0ffa2a972515" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9582267b-adc4-536b-9335-9619155f3b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-140646" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}37 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 52\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=8$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=5.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=64,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-64I & =\\begin{bmatrix}37 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 52\\end{bmatrix}-64\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-27 & -18 \\\\ -18 & -12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-64I)x=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =\\begin{bmatrix}37 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 52\\end{bmatrix}-25\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 27\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)x=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{16}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{15}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162017 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0d7f5df-a1f9-5242-9386-446313ec0178" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Columns of the First Matrix Given Part of a Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54deaa5d-b42c-582b-add4-d6575e45a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520120} {:answer/id #uuid "5adca1a5-04fa-5979-ab07-c4374ef39ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520132} {:answer/id #uuid "8584a18f-938b-5b11-9a92-aea06357491c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520185} {:answer/id #uuid "875c7469-79dd-5306-8869-1ae4d067e4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520190} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b0b4f8-5d8c-5df5-bcb5-6a41d1765e47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54deaa5d-b42c-582b-add4-d6575e45a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520120} :answer-field/id #uuid "50d8446e-fd5b-543b-bc96-f048b71511a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1290450b-3f65-5ec4-8f81-47e7a7dc9fcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95734" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A,$ $Σ,$ and $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the second column of $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${v}_{i}$ is the $i$th column of the matrix $V.$\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=6$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=4.$ Therefore, the second column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162018 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02dfe937-e604-5985-af6f-cdfa1a574ccd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Columns of the Third Matrix Given Part of a Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8816896f-cca6-5ce2-bf30-8d2b1f66e3f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371292} {:answer/id #uuid "2e10c5b6-c997-5994-9093-7e45e10efbd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371293} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fea695-072e-5f95-902a-71d988e363cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371294} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd9c1a8-ef05-5de9-af7d-a1baeb76d255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371295} {:answer/id #uuid "5b42e903-5007-58dd-9a44-08bf6ca76aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8816896f-cca6-5ce2-bf30-8d2b1f66e3f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371292} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aac91f8-948d-551f-bd8b-56bc67976e79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa5f61d9-1d7f-5da9-9527-e7cc3f414c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-95904" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}{v}_{11} & {v}_{12} \\\\ {v}_{21} & {v}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the value of $|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|?$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ the columns of $V$ must be the right singular vectors of $A,$ i.e., the unit eigenvectors of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=10$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=4.$ So, the first column of $V$ corresponds to the singular value ${\\sigma }_{1}=10.$\n\nHence, we need to find a unit eigenvector of ${A}^{T}\\,A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=100.$ \n\n- Computing ${A}^{T}\\,A,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}58 & 42 \\\\ 42 & 58\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Computing ${A}^{T}\\,A-100I,$ we get\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,A-100I=\\begin{bmatrix}58 & 42 \\\\ 42 & 58\\end{bmatrix}-100\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-42 & 42 \\\\ 42 & -42\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Seeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-100I)v=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|{v}_{11}|+|{v}_{21}|=|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|+|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9466d5b-d361-5504-8e16-99f87210e808" :knowledge-point/title "The Singular Value Decomposition of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2efb8c-2656-5a9e-bdf4-74177ad5bfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520055} {:answer/id #uuid "ab956e6c-1981-5cd4-973f-cb9d389db8f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520225} {:answer/id #uuid "ada77caf-e98c-55fb-aefb-f3d728826900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520230} {:answer/id #uuid "dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520302} {:answer/id #uuid "e183294d-0160-5657-9a79-b2a38d4cd596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dafadf4d-f436-5d63-ba00-63f2baf56d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520302} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef2ffd-6bce-5a3c-9878-3c95874f4572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eeba80ad-bee9-5269-baef-fbd3bd2d6cda" :question/math-academy-id "q-96323" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-81I & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-81[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -24 \\\\ -24 & -72\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-81I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-I & =[\\begin{aligned}73 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}72 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{27}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162019 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9466d5b-d361-5504-8e16-99f87210e808" :knowledge-point/title "The Singular Value Decomposition of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6eff25-c0fc-5cff-b89a-ea3df60bc57a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371383} {:answer/id #uuid "e891c291-46bc-51cc-90f8-4be4297699d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371384} {:answer/id #uuid "34122363-16d9-56df-9b3f-b02634a9a8a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371385} {:answer/id #uuid "f39d2e74-50cb-5515-aa8a-3fb01d053a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371386} {:answer/id #uuid "0a333ced-2bf0-5916-b1d2-6bcfa569537f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c6eff25-c0fc-5cff-b89a-ea3df60bc57a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371383} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c6dbf7-365b-568c-b7a1-8cd4a51005ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371382}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f93258a8-eb4b-5688-9b20-35af35814e98" :question/math-academy-id "q-96354" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=3.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 17\\end{bmatrix}-25\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-9I & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 17\\end{bmatrix}-9\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-9I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}]}
